🤝 Contributing
Contributions are welcome! This is a practice/learning project.

Fork the repo

Create feature branch (git checkout -b feature/amazing-feature)

Commit changes (git commit -m 'Add amazing feature')

Push to branch (git push origin feature/amazing-feature)

Open Pull Request

Coding Standards
Backend: PEP 8, type hints, docstrings

Frontend: ESLint + Prettier

Commits: Conventional commits (feat:, fix:, docs:)

🐛 Known Limitations
⚠️ Simulation models are simplified math (not real GIS data)

⚠️ SQLite not suitable for > 1000 concurrent users (migrate to PostgreSQL for production)

⚠️ Gemini API has rate limits (60/min on free tier)

⚠️ Map uses OpenStreetMap (no satellite imagery)

⚠️ No user authentication yet (all simulations are public)

These are intentional — this is a practice project, not production.

