🚀 Setup Guide
Prerequisites
Python 3.11+ installed

Node.js 18+ installed

Google Gemini API key (get free here)

Git installed

Step 1: Clone the Repository
bash
git clone https://github.com/vishakha2121/urbanmind-ai.git
cd urbanmind-ai
Step 2: Backend Setup
bash
# Navigate to backend
cd backend

# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate (Windows)
venv\Scripts\activate

# Activate (Mac/Linux)
source venv/bin/activate

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Create .env file
copy .env.example .env
# (Mac/Linux: cp .env.example .env)

# Edit .env and add your Gemini API key
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_key_here

# Run backend
uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000
Backend will be live at http://localhost:8000
API docs at http://localhost:8000/docs

Step 3: Frontend Setup
bash
# Open new terminal, navigate to frontend
cd frontend

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Create .env file
copy .env.example .env
# (Mac/Linux: cp .env.example .env)

# Run frontend
npm run dev
Frontend will be live at http://localhost:5173

Step 4: Get Gemini API Key (Free)
Go to https://ai.google.dev/

Click "Get API Key"

Sign in with Google account

Create new API key

Copy and paste into backend/.env:

text
GEMINI_API_KEY=AIzaSy...your_key_here
Free tier limits: 60 requests/minute, 1500 requests/day — more than enough.

📡 API Endpoints
Health Check
http
GET /api/health
Create Simulation
http
POST /api/simulations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "city_name": "Greenfield",
  "population": 50000,
  "area_sqkm": 25,
  "budget_crore": 500
}
Response:

json
{
  "id": 1,
  "city_name": "Greenfield",
  "population": 50000,
  "area_sqkm": 25,
  "budget_crore": 500,
  "overall_score": 68.5,
  "status": "completed",
  "agent_results": [...],
  "recommendations": {...},
  "created_at": "2024-01-15T10:30:00"
}
List All Simulations
http
GET /api/simulations?limit=10&offset=0
Get Simulation by ID
http
GET /api/simulations/{id}
Delete Simulation
http
DELETE /api/simulations/{id}
Get Recommendations Only
http
GET /api/simulations/{id}/recommendations
Full API documentation: Visit /docs when backend is running.

🧪 Testing
Run Backend Tests
bash
cd backend
pytest -v
Test Individual Agents
bash
pytest tests/test_agents.py -v
Test API Endpoints
bash
pytest tests/test_api.py -v
Manual API Testing
Use Postman or curl:

bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/simulations \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"city_name":"Test","population":50000,"area_sqkm":25,"budget_crore":500}'
